<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Compile Time on Beyond Swift</title><link>https://beyondswift.com/tags/compile-time/</link><description>Recent content in Compile Time on Beyond Swift</description><generator>Hugo -- 0.163.3</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 03:07:00 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://beyondswift.com/tags/compile-time/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Reading the build log for the slow line</title><link>https://beyondswift.com/understanding-build-logs-without-panic-scrolling/</link><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 03:07:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://beyondswift.com/understanding-build-logs-without-panic-scrolling/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;One-line change, incremental build, and one file sits at the compiler for forty seconds. The build log scrolls past a thousand lines and the only summary it gives you is &lt;code&gt;CompileSwiftSources&lt;/code&gt; took a while. Which line? It will not say.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Somewhere in that file is an expression like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; label = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Order &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; id &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; name &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34; x&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; String(qty)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34; = &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; String(price &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; quantity) &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34; &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; currencyCode
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reads fine. Compiles. And on its own it can cost the type-checker several seconds. The question is which expression, and the default log never points at it. By the end you will know the two flags that make the compiler name the slow line, and the one that names the slow phase.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>